I would, with the greatest respect, take issue with one point made by
Nicolas Brouard in his recent mailing; he said:

>>> As LaTeX 2.09 will be european, and will allow language specific
>>> styles, I think that the mechanism of hyphenation patterns loading
>>> HAS TO BE INCORPORATED. It has to be compatible with TeX 2.0, but
                            =
=08=08=08=08=08=08=08=08=08=08=08=08=08=08=08=08=08=08=08=08=08=08=08=08=08=
=08=08=08=08=08=08=08=08=08=08=08
>>> will offer the facility of reading 8 bits patterns if TeX 3 is
>>> available.

I belive that this is a totally unnecessary restriction.  TeX V3.x has
now been out for sufficiently long that all new development work should
be entitled to assume that it will be used; to continue to develop code
that maintains backwards-compatibility with TeX V2 is restricting, and =
may
well prevent the `best' code from being written.

					** Phil.


